# tools/fora_reconfig_witness.rish — change the constellation safely, through joint consensus (FORA13).
#
# Season: the Six-Season double-seat, Season D thread (Kresfa & Mycelium — the tree's own consensus) · waymark FORA · rung
# FORA13. Design read: active-designing/20260814-055235_fora13-constel-joint-consensus-reconfig.md
# Law kin: .claude/rules/placeholder-ship-names.md — the border guards every vote: a reconfiguration's replies deframe at the
# naming-law border (wire.deframe), so a real address can never enter a transition even as a present token.
#
# constel/reconfig.rye closes the blind spot FORA12's log left open: the fixed-roster no-fork proof holds only while the
# membership never changes. Reconfiguration is the single hardest move a consensus protocol makes — during a switch from an old
# config C_old to a new one C_new, two disjoint groups (one under each config) could each form a lawful majority and commit
# conflicting values, a fork born of the change itself. Joint consensus closes it with one bounded rule that spends the FORA9
# intersection lemma directly: a transition decision requires a strict majority in BOTH C_old and C_new. Because any two strict
# majorities of a config intersect, a joint decision overlaps any pure-old and any pure-new decision — so the reconfiguration
# inherits the whole no-fork guarantee. The selftest proves: a joint majority in both configs commits; an old-only or new-only
# majority refuses NoJointMajority; NO FORK ACROSS THE SWITCH, enumerated directly (every joint-majority yes-set intersects
# every pure-old majority inside old and every pure-new majority inside new); DoubleVote, NotInEitherConfig, and EmptyConfig
# each refuse by name; the border guards every vote (VowelPresent at hear); and a full transition over eight stays bounded.
# Purely local — no socket, no network, no keys, no funds, no real address ever formed.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/fora_reconfig_witness.rish

say "fora-reconfig: Language EN — FORA13 lets the constellation add and lose piers without a fork: a transition commits only with a strict majority in BOTH the old and new membership, so no two disjoint groups can ever each decide a conflicting value across the switch."
say "fora-reconfig: Style Radiant — a sky that can never change its stars is a painting, not a constellation; joint consensus lets Constel reconfigure with the same no-fork promise the fixed log already keeps."
say "fora-reconfig: Lens TAME — the decision is bounded (majority in each config, refusing NoJointMajority below either), every config non-empty by construction (EmptyConfig), a pier votes once (DoubleVote) and only if it participates (NotInEitherConfig); the round interleaves respond and hear so a full transition never risks ChannelFull; siloed to constel/, run from inside the jailed pier; no socket, no network, no keys, no funds, no real address ever formed (custody gate #2 and gate #4 untouched)."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "constel/bin/reconfig"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p constel/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build constel/reconfig.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "fora-reconfig: build failed — ${build.err}"

let outfile = "constel/bin/reconfig.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "fora-reconfig: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "fora-reconfig: ${shown.out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN fora-reconfig' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "fora-reconfig: selftest did not print the GREEN fora-reconfig line"

say "fora-reconfig: GREEN — the sky can change its stars without a fork; the constel consensus track can now safely reconfigure its own membership, proven pure on the bench, the one Comlink-socket rung still the maintainer's own hand."
